# The seed CSVs are hashed byte-for-byte against docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md and
# scripts/seed-manifest.ts (which in turn trace to the SHA-256 published in the case study brief).
# core.autocrlf on a contributor's machine (Windows commonly defaults this to true) would silently
# rewrite LF to CRLF on checkout and break every one of those hashes. Force these files to be
# treated as binary — no line-ending conversion, ever, on any platform, in either direction.
seed/*.csv -text

# Everything else: normalise to LF in the repo, checked out as LF everywhere. Consistent hashes,
# consistent diffs, no autocrlf surprises for contributors on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf
